# TypeScript SDK conventions

## Layout (mirror TRD)

- `src/contracts/` — public SDK types + internal adapter contracts (`sdk`, `adapter`, `events`, `messages`, `lifecycle`, `operations`, `capabilities`)
- `src/core/` — `runtime-manager`, registries, `event-bus` (no Telegram provider imports)
- `src/adapters/telegram/` — resolver, `mtproto/`, `bot-api/`, capabilities
- `src/errors/` — typed error hierarchy from PRD/TRD
- `src/observability/` — `Logger`, noop implementation
- `src/utils/` — validators, timeout/abort, retry helpers
- `tests/unit/`, `tests/contract/`, `examples/`

## Public API

- Stable facade: `TelegramRuntimeSdk` (register/start/stop bots, subscriptions, `sendMessage`, `onMessage` / `onError` / `onBotStateChange`).
- Async operations accept `OperationOptions` (`timeoutMs`, `signal`) where specified in TRD.
- Bot lifecycle states: `registered` | `starting` | `started` | `stopping` | `stopped` | `error` — honor transition rules and idempotency tables in PRD §11.2 / TRD §7.7.

## Quality bar

- No `any` on exported public types.
- Unit tests for core; contract tests for adapter behavior (lifecycle, bind/unbind, send chat/topic, error mapping).
